/// ✅ FIXED (2026-07-14, iter 43) — siblings `@…` (tuple/list) + `@b2af1244` (record field) completed the
/// tail-resumptive fold for a perform in a heap-COMPOUND constructor element. `run` below now COMPILES and
/// runs correctly (the tuple `(Fresh.next(), Fresh.next())` → (0, 1), `0 + 1` = 1). Kept as a REGRESSION
/// WITNESS. The original iter-38 finding follows for history.
///
/// ORIGINAL (iter 38 — DECLINE, now resolved): performing an effect operation directly as an ELEMENT of a
/// heap-COMPOUND constructor (tuple / list / record) was NOT reducible by the tail-resumptive handler fold:
///   error: "this handler is not yet reducible by the tail-resumptive fold (cross-function or non-tail
///           resume arrives in a later increment)"
/// A perform in an arith operand / call arg / sum-ctor payload always worked; the compound-constructor
/// element was the gap, now closed for tuple, list, AND record fields.
///
/// SHARP BOUNDARY (mapped iter 38) — the trigger is the CONSTRUCTOR-ELEMENT position, and it needs NO
/// recursion:
///   DECLINES:  let p = (Fresh.next(), Fresh.next()) in …   -- perform in a TUPLE element (this file)
///              let xs = [Fresh.next(), Fresh.next()] in …  -- perform in a LIST element
///              let r = { a = Fresh.next() } in …           -- perform in a RECORD field
///              (even a SINGLE perform element, even with no recursion, even projected directly).
///   WORKS:     Fresh.next() + Fresh.next()                 -- perform in an ARITH operand
///              twice(Fresh.next())                         -- perform as a CALL argument
///              W.Mk(Fresh.next())                          -- perform in a SUM ctor payload
///              let r = Fresh.next() in go(n - 1, acc + r)  -- perform let-bound, tail self-call
///              let a = Fresh.next() in let b = Fresh.next() in (a, b)  -- PREFETCH then construct
///
/// WORKAROUND (what a real pass does anyway, so this rarely bites in practice): bind each perform to a
/// `let` FIRST, then build the tuple/list/record from the bound variables (the last WORKS line). The gap
/// is only that the fold does not itself hoist a perform out of a tuple/list/record element position — it
/// already hoists the arith-operand / call-arg / sum-payload cases. Fix locus: extend the reducible set in
/// `effects.rs` to a perform in a `Tuple`/`ListNew`/`Record` element (hoist like the cases it handles).
effect Fresh =
  | next : -> Int64

/// The declining shape: two performs as tuple elements (no recursion needed).
def go() =
  let p = (Fresh.next(), Fresh.next()) in
  p.0 + p.1

def run() =
  handle Fresh(0) with
    | next(s) => resume(s, s + 1)
  in
  go()

export { run }
